<%#
# Сводка

The state of the platform at a glance. The header is drawn here, and so are the body parts that cost nothing to draw: the tiles with
the headline figures, the list «Нужно проверить» and the reminder about two-factor sign-in. The table of accounts «Подробно по
каналам» and the chart are the Vue component DashboardIndex.

## Local variables (controller instance variables):

- `@summary`: the figures of the tiles (SuperAdmin::DashboardSummary); the chart of conversations is `@summary[:chart]`.
- `@checklist`: the list «Нужно проверить» (SuperAdmin::DashboardChecklist): the alerts of SuperAdmin::DashboardAlerts and the
  problems of the accounts in one list.
- `@health_accounts`, `@health_summary`: one row per account and the totals (SuperAdmin::HealthMatrixService);
  `@health_summary[:updated_at]` is already Astana time.
%>

<% content_for(:title) do %><%= t('super_admin.dashboard.title') %><% end %>

<%# The Vue bundle is needed only here; the layout prints it in <head> via `yield :vue_entry`. %>
<% content_for(:vue_entry) do %>
  <%= vite_javascript_tag 'superadmin_pages' %>
<% end %>

<%= render layout: 'super_admin/shared/page_header', locals: { title: content_for(:title), description: t('super_admin.dashboard.description') } do %>
  <% if @health_summary[:updated_at].present? %>
    <span class="text-xs tabular-nums text-n-slate-11"><%= t('super_admin.dashboard.updated', time: @health_summary[:updated_at]) %></span>
  <% end %>
  <%= link_to super_admin_root_path(refresh: true), class: 'button button--secondary' do %>
    <span class="i-lucide-refresh-cw size-4" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <%= t('super_admin.dashboard.refresh') %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<section class="main-content__body">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-5">
    <%= render 'tiles', summary: @summary, attention: @checklist.total %>
    <%# What needs a look first: trials, disk space, the OpenRouter key, the queues, channels, telephony, MedElement. %>
    <%= render 'checklist', checklist: @checklist %>
    <%= render 'super_admin/shared/two_factor_notice', super_admin: current_super_admin %>
    <%= render_vue_component('DashboardIndex', {
      chartData: @summary[:chart],
      healthAccounts: @health_accounts,
      healthSummary: @health_summary
    }) %>
  </div>
</section>
